{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the festival.</b> It is written in two places, and there [it says] 'at the going out of the year,' for the end of the year is the beginning of the other year, and this is a sign that the sun enters the constellation of Libra near the day of the equinox, and it will not be delayed until the going out of Sukkot, so that the other year has not yet begun; therefore it is written 'the turning of the year.' And do not rely on the cycle of Shmuel, only on the cycle of Rav Ada, even though it requires two corrections: the first, because the sun's motion is sometimes longer and sometimes shorter, and this variation is not in the sun's motion, for it is always uniform, but only relative to the appearance of the point on the sphere of the zodiac; and the second correction is on account of the motion of a small sphere at the head of Aries."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:23.299353907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}